    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0727" n="631" xml:id="pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.6363/1765</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sheffield</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                        1926</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 804</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am enclosing herewith for immediate
                    delivery to the Minister for Foreign Affairs the original of my Note to him of
                    March 1 in answer to his Note to me dated February 12. There is enclosed as well
                    an office copy for your files. As telegraphed to you, I have today handed a copy
                    of this Note to Ambassador Téllez, who has stated that he will telegraph it to
                    his Government; whether merely a summary or in full, I, of course, am not in a
                    position to say.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank B. Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d378-a1.xml" xpointer="d378-a1"/>
            </div>
